  "construction": "Reversing fold of a pair-partition CPM CSS code of arXiv:2609.30069 with J = 3, L = 10, P = 14. Parent qubit q = c*P + t. Parent X row (j,s) meets c*P + ((s - E[j][c]) mod P) for each block c. The involution is pi(c*P + t) = sigma[c]*P + ((-t - B[sigma[c]]) mod P). Folded site i pairs the i-th smallest q with q < pi(q) with pi(q). Each parent X row becomes one generator, X where it meets a representative and Z where it meets a partner. E = [[8, 3, 11, 0, 7, 6, 12, 8, 13, 1], [7, 13, 6, 6, 9, 4, 13, 2, 3, 4], [2, 3, 3, 12, 8, 9, 9, 10, 6, 11]], sigma = [6, 7, 3, 2, 8, 9, 0, 1, 4, 5], B = [12, 5, 1, 1, 1, 5, 12, 5, 1, 5].",
